      "body": "Northstar Health Plan Appeals\nappeals@northstarhealth.example\n\nRe: Appeal of Balance Billing - Claim CN77310452, Member ID NSH884217353\nPatient: Jane Doe\nProvider: Mercy Valley Hospital\nDate of Service: 2026-05-06\nEOB Notice Date: 2026-05-20\nProvider Account: MV-2290417\n\nDear Appeals Department,\n\nI am writing to formally appeal the balance billing on the above-referenced claim. The hospital statement dated 2026-06-03 demands $2,840.00, but your Explanation of Benefits dated 2026-05-20 shows my patient responsibility is only $412.00. The difference of $2,428.00 represents the amount the in-network provider is contractually required to write off.\n\nClaim details per the EOB (Claim CN77310452):\n- CPT 99283 (Emergency dept visit, level 3): Billed $1,640.00, Allowed $250.00, Patient responsibility $250.00\n- CPT 73610 (X-ray ankle, 3 views): Billed $480.00, Allowed $62.00, Patient responsibility $62.00\n- CPT 29515 (Short-leg splint application): Billed $720.00, Allowed $100.00, Patient responsibility $100.00\n- Total billed: $2,840.00\n- Total allowed: $412.00\n- Total patient responsibility per EOB: $412.00\n\nThe hospital bill incorrectly charges the full billed amount of $2,840.00 with $0.00 contractual adjustments, contrary to the in-network agreement reflected on the EOB which states \"in-network providers may not bill the difference between billed and allowed amounts.\"\n\nThis appeal is filed within the 180-day window (EOB notice date 2026-05-20; appeal deadline 2026-11-16).\n\nI respectfully request that you:\n1. Provide written confirmation that my account with Mercy Valley Hospital is adjusted to the EOB patient responsibility of $412.00.\n2. Direct the provider to hold this account from collections during review.\n3. Respond to this appeal within 30 days.\n\nThe EOB and hospital statement are available on request.\n\nSincerely,\nJane Doe\nMember ID: NSH884217353",
