          "response_time": 2.51,
          "answer": "Under the ACA, most health insurance plans allow 180 days from the denial notice to file an internal appeal. This is confirmed by multiple sources, including coverage-rights.com, meritsappeals.com, appealgen.com, HealthCare.gov, and the CMS document. For urgent medical situations, insurers must issue a decision within 72 hours. Some states require longer deadlines, such as Florida which requires 365 days. Always check your specific denial letter for your exact deadline.",
