          "response_time": 2.61,
          "answer": "The sources indicate that the allowed amount in ACA marketplace health plans refers to the negotiated or lowered price agreed upon between the healthcare provider and the insurer, which is the maximum cost the insurer reimburses the provider. The contractual adjustment is the difference between the billed amount and the allowed amount, which is written off by the provider and not billed to the patient. The sources do not provide specific figures for the contractual adjustment amount in in-network provider scenarios under ACA marketplace health plans.",
